1
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:09,550
A sailmaker is making a triangular sail.

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,620
Its base is 4 metres, and its height is 6 metres.

3
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,380
How much fabric is needed?

4
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:19,990
Here is a hint: think about the rectangle that fits around the sail.

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,570
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:26,050
Draw a rectangle around the sail.

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:31,120
It is 4 metres by 6 metres, so its area is 24 square metres.

8
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:34,940
The triangle fills exactly half of the rectangle.

9
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,260
Half of 24 is 12.

10
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:40,090
The sail needs 12 square metres of fabric.

11
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:45,040
Remember: the area of a rectangle is the length times the width.

12
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:50,210
Any triangle fits inside a rectangle with the same base and the same height.

13
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:53,620
And it always takes up exactly half of it.

14
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:58,750
So the area of a triangle is a half, times the base, times the height.

15
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:04,270
The answer is in square units, like square centimetres or square metres.

16
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:04,970
Your turn.

17
00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:09,820
A triangle has a base of 9 centimetres and a height of 4 centimetres.

18
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:11,020
What is its area?

19
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:14,320
Pause the video and try it.

20
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:15,850
9 times 4 is 36.

21
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,470
Half of 36 is 18.

22
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:21,270
The area is 18 square centimetres.

23
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,310
The height must be perpendicular to the base.

24
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:27,420
That means it meets the base at a right angle.

25
00:01:27,470 --> 00:01:29,650
It is not a slanted side.

26
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:35,020
Any side can be the base, as long as you use the height that goes with it.

27
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:38,880
In some triangles, the height falls outside the triangle.

28
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:42,620
You still use a half, times base, times height.

29
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:43,980
Here is the method.

30
00:01:44,030 --> 00:01:46,110
Step 1: choose a base.

31
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:50,350
Step 2: find the perpendicular height to that base.

32
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,460
Step 3: work out a half, times base, times height.

33
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:58,880
Step 4: ignore any slanted side that is not the height.

34
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:04,510
A right-angled triangle has shorter sides of 9 centimetres and 6 centimetres.

35
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,080
Find its area.

36
00:02:06,130 --> 00:02:08,980
The 2 shorter sides meet at a right angle.

37
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:12,840
So one is the base, and the other is the height.

38
00:02:12,890 --> 00:02:17,410
A half times 9 times 6 is 27 square centimetres.

39
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:26,310
A triangle has a base of 14 centimetres, a slanted side of 11 centimetres, and a perpendicular height of 9 centimetres.

40
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,910
Find its area.

41
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:30,530
Use the base, 14, and the height, 9.

42
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:33,110
Do not use the slanted side.

43
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:37,910
A half times 14 times 9 is 63 square centimetres.

44
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:43,580
A triangle has an area of 36 square centimetres, and a base of 9 centimetres.

45
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:45,300
Find its height.

46
00:02:45,350 --> 00:02:47,410
Half of the base is 4.5.

47
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:50,590
So 4.5 times the height is 36.

48
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,670
36 divided by 4.5 is 8.

49
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:55,750
The height is 8 centimetres.

50
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,490
Your turn.

51
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:02,240
A triangle has an area of 40 square centimetres, and a base of 16 centimetres.

52
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:03,640
What is its height?

53
00:03:03,690 --> 00:03:07,040
Pause the video and try it.

54
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:08,410
Half of 16 is 8.

55
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,810
So 8 times the height is 40.

56
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:15,980
The height is 40 divided by 8, which is 5 centimetres.

57
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:18,230
A sign has the shape of a house.

58
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:22,720
It is a rectangle, 8 metres by 5 metres, with a triangle on top.

59
00:03:22,770 --> 00:03:27,550
The triangle has a base of 8 metres and a height of 3 metres.

60
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:31,760
The rectangle is 8 times 5, which is 40 square metres.

61
00:03:31,810 --> 00:03:37,460
The triangle is a half times 8 times 3, which is 12 square metres.

62
00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:38,160
Add them.

63
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:41,430
The total area is 52 square metres.

64
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:49,170
A triangle has a base of 12 centimetres, a sloping side of 15 centimetres, and a height of 9 centimetres.

65
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:50,200
Find its area.

66
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:51,830
Here is Ana's working.

67
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,260
Is it right?

68
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:54,470
Line 1 is wrong.

69
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:57,120
15 centimetres is the sloping side.

70
00:03:57,170 --> 00:04:00,310
It is not the perpendicular height.

71
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,860
Use the height, 9.

72
00:04:01,910 --> 00:04:06,630
A half times 12 times 9 is 54 square centimetres.

73
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:11,130
Each face of the Great Pyramid in Egypt is a huge triangle.

74
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:13,350
Its base is about 230 metres.

75
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:18,090
Its height, measured up the slope, is about 186 metres.

76
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:24,690
A half times 230 times 186 is about 21,400 square metres.

77
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:29,040
That is more than 2 hectares of stone, on just 1 face.

78
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:30,340
One last question.

79
00:04:30,390 --> 00:04:34,150
A right-angled triangle has shorter sides of 6 and 7.

80
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,370
What is its area?

81
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:38,710
Pause the video and answer.

82
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,280
6 times 7 is 42.

83
00:04:40,330 --> 00:04:41,950
Half of 42 is 21.

84
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,240
The area is 21 square units.

85
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:52,140
To remember: the area of a triangle is a half, times the base, times the perpendicular height.

86
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:55,380
The height is at right angles to the base.

87
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:59,340
Any side can be the base, with its matching height.

88
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:03,180
Work backwards to find a missing base or height.

89
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:08,630
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.3 on Camday.
